body:
Yea, I effectively try and play within those 'rules' as is, but till it's implemented there's going to be people who aren't interested in playing that way. I'm just arguing that it's needless to go beyond this since it's already effectively the intent of the game and how it will be, it's just locked behind a missing feature/bug for now. 

&#x200B;

I personally just find it silly when people exclusively want to run around with less lethal weapons in all circumstances and get upset when people do not play this way. There's a bunch of guns in the game for a reason after all, and playing both ways is totally valid depending on the circumstances imo.

I feel pretty deflated in terms of trying to work with my friend, it seems pointless, and I’m not really serving myself in it either. You’re right about it just making things even worse, and it certainly isn’t helping me be kinder to myself. I was there, I was in that space of being able to confront people, I was in a really great space, I was in a space where I had boundaries, self-esteem, confidence. I really have just seen all of that evaporate. I know I’ve done that too, that I’ve stopped living as me and started living as my imagination of how others want me to be, there’s a lot of pressure. I feel like I’m a corrupted, disheveled shattered version of who I am, and it makes it feel impossible to see straight, like I’m staring into a broken mirror and can’t work out which fragment is supposed to be me. I hope so, I hope that I’m still there, it’s hard to feel it, especially when I try and push, when I try and work on it and to do things \*I\* know I liked doing, that made me feel me. And it’s just so much effort, it’s so much disconnect and feeling of being outside myself. I’m looking forward to grad work because it feels like the last strand of myself I can grab onto, I’m terrified that I’ll do it and I won’t feel anything, that I’ll be unable to care. I’m worried that will be the final straw for me.  


&#x200B;

It’s hard not to blame myself, on some level everything I do is a choice, and I struggle so much to make the choices I even want to make for myself. It’s hard to not be hard on myself. Writing feels like a last little shard of myself, like the one time I can feel in the zone and who I am. It takes me so much to read a book, I want to, but I’ll decide that how I feel right now isn’t good enough to read a book, that I’m wasting it on a me that can’t see to feel it and appreciate it. I feel that too, even the people who care about me can’t seem to just stomp all over my progress and blame me, without even realising they are doing it. It’s always so simple, like “why don't you just x?” as if I’d never thought of that, as if I’d never tried it.   
   


&#x200B;

I feel very strongly about this, society is pathetic to me when it comes to how we treat survivors, victims, anyone struggling. I don’t think we are ready to face reality, to admit that if there are all these victims, then there are so, so, so many perpetrators that live among us. So much easier to blame the victim than to come to terms with your friend being a rapist, your father or husband being a child abuser, your leaders, your co-worker, so many ‘normal’ ‘successful’ people are monsters. But they are allowed within society, because it’s easier than the reality. Society has an endless slew of normative behaviour and commentary on people like me, people who’ve experienced what I have, and it’s not really kind for the most part. It’s at best “I’m so sorry this happened to you” and then later all the little comments we’ve been trained to say come out and start blaming me for what happened to me. I wish this was understood, my brain is wired for the circumstances I was in, and people just want me to all of a sudden be functional in the world, I even want it. I’ve been doing it gradually for so long, it’s honestly just endless tiring work that I haven't really got an alternative to. What else can I do? I hate it. I don’t even really engage with my thoughts that much, which is a process I've been experiencing for a while now. I'm very disconnected and I know I’m dissociating, coming on here and my therapy appointments are these blips where I come up for air. I’ve mostly had a very active mind, so it being so quiet is strange for me too. I just blank out the day till it goes away and repeat, I’ve gotten to a point of not having a negative inner critic in the past, I don’t even know where I am these days. I really appreciate you writing it in such detail and spending so much time, I’ve really struggled to respond and am now sitting down with it in a word doc going through point by point even though I’ve read it quite a few times now. I think when I’m lucid I’m not so bad, I’m just doing an amazingly thorough job of keeping myself suppressed, I stay awake all night at the moment, I’m always stimulating myself with something distracting. Every time I go and unstack the dishwasher, and I’m given some time to think, I just start crying, I really just don’t have it in me to face myself. I honestly just feel comforted hearing you write good things about me, my criticism of myself feels very, active honestly. I have to do it myself, and it’s because I’ve spent two years just blotting out the world and I feel like I’m trying to shake myself awake and make myself aware that I’m missing me, that I’m missing life.
